<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Janusz Radziwiłł (1579–1620)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1579–1620</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/janusz-radziwill">Janusz Radziwiłł</a> was a Lithuanian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/magnates">magnate</a> of the Calvinist branch of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/radziwill-family">Radziwiłł family</a>. In 1600 he married <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sophia-olelkovich">Sophia Olelkovich</a>, heiress of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slutsk">Slutsk</a>, bringing the duchy to the Radziwiłłs. He was one of the leaders of the Zebrzydowski Rebellion against King Sigismund III in 1606–1607 and later became castellan of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vilnius">Vilnius</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/janusz-radziwill-1579-1620.jpg" alt="Janusz Radziwiłł (1579–1620)" width="320" height="384" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:POL_Janusz_Radziwill_(1579-1620).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
